   "source": [
    "### Query 5: How do the tax credit modifications under the US \"One Big Beautiful Bill Act\" (OBBBA) affect the investment economics of using domestic versus imported feedstocks for Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF), and what cascading impact will this biofuel transition have on the capacity rationalisation of traditional US West Coast refineries?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 38,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "**Headline Finding:** The US \"One Big Beautiful Bill Act\" (OBBBA) modifies tax credits to favor domestic feedstocks for Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF), making imported feedstocks less competitive.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Supporting Data:** The OBBBA reduces the 45Z tax credits by 43% for SAFs and eliminates tax credits for SAFs produced from imported feedstocks, except for those from Canada and Mexico [Renewables2025 p.160]. As a result, imported SAFs and SAFs made from imported feedstocks will receive almost 60% less total support, making them largely uncompetitive [Renewables2025 p.160].\n",
      "\n",
      "**Cross-Sector Linkages:** The shift towards domestic feedstocks for SAF production may lead to increased demand for domestic biofuels and feedstocks, potentially raising feedstock costs and putting pressure on margins [Renewables2025 p.148]. This, in turn, may impact the capacity rationalization of traditional US West Coast refineries as they adapt to changing market dynamics.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Countervailing Forces:** The proposed RFS updates and California's plans to strengthen Low Carbon Fuel Standard targets may maintain demand signals for biofuels, including SAF [Renewables2025 p.148]. However, uncertainty remains considerable due to the lack of final RFS rules and additional details on the 45Z tax credit [Renewables2025 p.148]. New trade developments, such as the revised trade agreement between the UK and the US, may also influence producer decisions [Renewables2025 p.148].\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Strategy: tuned_rag  \u2014  benchmark query 5\n",
    "answer = CACHED_ANSWERS['tuned_rag']['answers'][4]\n",
    "print(answer)\n"
   ]
